LICENSE / LICENSING NOTICE
==========================

This repository (raouldekezel/dolphin-robot) is a fork of the upstream project:

    https://github.com/sh00t2kill/dolphin-robot

Upstream licensing status
-------------------------

As of 2026-07-13, the upstream repository does not publish a LICENSE file.
Under default copyright rules, the original work is therefore "all rights
reserved" by its authors, and no license terms are available to be inherited
by this fork.

Consequently, this fork makes NO license grant covering the upstream code.
All rights in the original work remain with the upstream authors and
contributors, including @sh00t2kill, @lordlala and @elad-bar as listed in
`custom_components/mydolphin_plus/manifest.json`.

Fork-specific modifications
---------------------------

Modifications, additions, tests, documentation and diagnostic material
contributed in this fork by @raouldekezel are published with no intentions
beyond the author's education and personal use. No separate or conflicting
terms are asserted over them, and they carry no claim over the upstream work
they derive from.

Intended use
------------

This fork exists to develop and test changes against real Maytronics Dolphin
hardware, with no intentions beyond the author's education and personal use.
It is not intended as an independent redistribution of the upstream work, and
it is not published in the HACS default store.

Trademarks and brand assets
---------------------------

"Maytronics", "Dolphin" and "MyDolphin Plus" are trademarks of their
respective owners. The brand image shipped under
`custom_components/mydolphin_plus/brand/` is the same asset already published
for the `mydolphin_plus` domain in the `home-assistant/brands` repository, and
is used solely for identification purposes within the Home Assistant user
interface, as permitted by the Home Assistant brands policy.

Note to upstream
----------------

Should the upstream maintainers publish an explicit license for
sh00t2kill/dolphin-robot (MIT is the de-facto norm for Home Assistant custom
integrations), this notice will be replaced by those terms.
